" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050469 #edb/ref 1033 726 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050469 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "4c3afa77-0505-5a1a-9d73-711526ff20ea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082985 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4058" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082985 #edb/ref 1071 "Express the equation $10^3 = 1\\,000$ using logarithmic notation." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082985 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "057534f6-5144-57c1-ade0-1693dffa44e2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082985 #edb/ref 1074 "The common logarithm of $a$ is defined as follows:\n\n$a = 10^x$ is equivalent to $\\log{a} = x$\n\nIf we compare $10^3 = 1\\,000$ with $10^x = a,$ we get that $a = 1\\,000$ and $x = 3.$\n\nTherefore, the given equation can be expressed as $\\log{1\\,000} = 3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082986 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4059" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082986 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $\\log\\left( 10^{7}\\right).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082986 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e9e02baa-a9bc-5f3f-af29-2bbac1dc2634" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082986 #edb/ref 1074 "The common logarithm of a power of $10$ is the power itself:\n\n$$\n\\log\\left(10^x\\right) = x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $x =7.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\log\\left( 10^{7}\\right) = 7.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082987 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4060" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082987 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $\\log\\left( 0.1 \\right).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082987 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "34a604f1-d3e2-5746-818a-17c572ff2243" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082987 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we rewrite $0.1$ as a power of $10$ (the base of the common logarithm) as follows:\n\n$$\n0.1 = 10^{-1}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\log\\left( 0.1 \\right) = \\log\\left(10^{-1}\\right).\n$$\n\nThe common logarithm of a power of $10$ is the power itself:\n\n$$\n\\log\\left(10^x\\right) = x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $x = -1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\log\\left( 10^{-1} \\right)= -1.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082988 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4061" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082988 #edb/ref 1071 "Rounded to $2$ decimal places, what is the value of $2\\log(7) + 5\\log(5)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082988 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b4b8a7af-fe7c-5d8a-80f4-c997c404a889" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082988 #edb/ref 1074 "We compute the required expression to $2$ decimal places using a calculator, rounding the intermediate steps to $5$ decimal places to avoid rounding error. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{log}⁡(7)+5\\operatorname{log}⁡(5) & ≈2(0.845\\,10)+5(0.698\\,97) \\\\  & =1.690\\,20+3.494\\,85 \\\\  & =5.185\\,05 \\\\  & ≈5.19.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083172 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049859 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083172 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049865 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083172 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083172 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083889 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083172 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234203 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083172 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234205 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083172 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186520513 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083172 #edb/ref 1039 "Converting Between Exponential and Logarithmic Form With Common Logarithms" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083172 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186082985 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083172 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "a81e85da-c4ce-5353-9a7b-d18daa4caf7d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083173 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048964 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083173 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083884 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083173 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083886 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083173 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083173 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234516 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083173 #