b/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520438 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186520022 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520438 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "eb5c14ac-5329-5c13-b0e7-0bc5f4c03d4d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520440 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520004 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520440 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520026 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520440 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520121 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520440 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520160 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520440 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520235 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520440 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520440 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520440 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186520160 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520440 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f3c10359-a725-56d7-95af-b4b16edd4bab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520448 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186520371 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520448 #edb/ref 1069 "q-78745" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520448 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520448 #edb/ref 1071 "Rounded to $3$ decimal places, find the value of $f(x)=3\\operatorname{log}⁡(2x)-2\\operatorname{log}⁡(5x)$ at $x=3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520448 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0714c123-409e-586b-bfd3-01ab5d4541d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520448 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we replace $x=3$ and get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3) & =3\\operatorname{log}⁡(2\\cdot 3)-2\\operatorname{log}⁡(5\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{log}⁡(6)-2\\operatorname{log}⁡(15)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe compute the required value to $3$ decimal places using a calculator, rounding the intermediate steps to $6$ decimal places to avoid rounding error. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3) & =3\\operatorname{log}⁡(6)-2\\operatorname{log}⁡(15) \\\\  & ≈3(0.778\\,151)-2(1.176\\,091) \\\\  & =2.334\\,453-2.352\\,182 \\\\  & =-0.017\\,729 \\\\  & ≈-0.018\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520450 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186520440 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520450 #edb/ref 1069 "q-66630" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520450 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520450 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{10})=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520450 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "091b6406-ea9f-5edd-85ff-748cd7849985" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520450 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we rewrite $\\sqrt[{}^{3}]{10}$ as a power of $10$ (the base of the common logarithm) as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{10}={10}^{1/3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{10})=\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{1/3})\n$$\n\nThe common logarithm reverses the action of the exponent. The principle is:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{x})=x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $x=\\frac{1}{3}.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{1/3})=\\frac{1}{3}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520469 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186520432 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520469 #edb/ref 1069 "q-99890" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520469 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520469 #edb/ref 1071 "Rounded to $3$ decimal places, $\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(8)}{3\\operatorname{log}⁡(11)}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520469 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5a64a8e4-76a1-5b39-9c41-0b568b095115" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520469 #edb/ref 1074 "We compute the required expression to $3$ decimal places using a calculator, rounding the intermediate steps to $6$ decimal places to avoid rounding error. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(8)}{3\\operatorname{log}⁡(11)} & ≈\\frac{0.903\\,090}{3(1.041\\,393)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.903\\,090}{3.124\\,179} \\\\  & ≈0.289\\,065 \\\\  & ≈0.289\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520498 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186520426 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520498 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108088" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520498 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520498 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\sqrt[5]{10})=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520498 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d37627d8-2221-5b06-8378-80d838ec2dc0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520498 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we rewrite $\\sqrt[5]{10}$ as a power of $10$ (the base of the common logarithm) as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[5]{10}={10}^{1/5}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\sqrt[5]{10})=\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{1/5})\n$$\n\nThe common logarithm reverses the action of the exponent. The principle is:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{x})=x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $x=\\frac{1}{5}.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{1/5})=\\frac{1}{5}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520505 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186520409 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520505 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108087" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520505 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520505 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the value of $2\\operatorname{log}⁡({t}^{3})-\\operatorname{log}⁡(10t)$ at $t=10.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520505 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e5c7ea95-c351-53b5-8952-0f4a790122f8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520505 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we substitute $t=10$ into the function. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{log}⁡({t}^{3})-\\operatorname{log}⁡(10t) & =2\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{3})-\\operatorname{log}⁡(10\\cdot 10) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{3})-\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe common logarithm reverses the action of the exponent. The principle is:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{x})=x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $x=3$ and $x=2.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{3})-\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{2})=2\\cdot 3-2=4\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520511 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186520438 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520511 #edb/ref 1069 "q-66628" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520511 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520511 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\operatorname{log}⁡(0.01)=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520511 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f698077a-723c-5eb7-8769-9b9cd991b10a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520511 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we rewrite $0.01$ as a power of $10$ (the base of the common logarithm) as follows:\n\n$$\n0.01={10}^{-2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡(0.01)=\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{-2})\n$$\n\nThe common logarithm reverses the action of the exponent. The principle is:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{x})=x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $x=-2.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{-2})=-2\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520513 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186520424 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520513 #edb/ref 1069 "q-66546" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520513 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520513 #edb/ref 1071 "What exponential equation is equivalent to the logarithmic equation $\\operatorname{log}⁡a=\\frac{1}{2}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520513 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f7974a75-c042-5467-9fad-57099eb48349" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520513 #edb/ref 1074 "The common logarithm of $a$ is defined as follows:\n\n$\\operatorname{log}⁡a=x$ is equivalent to $a={10}^{x}$\n\nIf we compare $\\operatorname{log}⁡a=\\frac{1}{2}$ with $\\operatorname{log}⁡a=x,$ we get that $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the given equation can be expressed as ${10}^{1/2}=a.$\n\nFinally, since ${10}^{1/2}=\\sqrt{10},$ the equation $\\operatorname{log}⁡a=\\frac{1}{2}$ is equivalent to $\\sqrt{10}=a.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
